WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.184
The school next asks you to recognize gastrointestinal bleeding and bowel obstruction. One can hide blood loss; the other can hide fluid loss inside a distended bowel.
学校接着要求识别胃肠出血及肠梗阻。前者可能隐藏失血，后者可能把液体丢失藏在扩张肠管内。

00:00:11.184 --> 00:00:23.064
Both can present with vomiting, pain, poor perfusion or reduced urine. The shared consequences do not make their cause, definitive treatment or medication choices identical.
两者都可呕吐、疼痛、低灌注或尿少，但共同后果并不使病因、确定治疗或用药选择相同。

00:00:23.064 --> 00:00:34.128
We will follow mechanisms, recognize red flags and build a safe assessment and conveyance plan. An exact source diagnosis is often unavailable in the field.
本课会沿机制识别红旗，建立安全评估和转运计划；现场往往无法取得确切来源诊断。

00:00:34.128 --> 00:00:46.944
Use the original unfolding cases and the assigned CPSC reading to connect the patient, visible findings and any existing devices. These are preparation, not school assessment answers.
利用原创展开病例及指定CPSC阅读，把患者、可见发现及已有器械连接起来；这些用于准备，不是学校考核答案。

00:00:46.944 --> 00:00:58.320
The school uses the classic ligament-of-Treitz boundary near the duodenojejunal junction. Upper sources include the esophagus, stomach and duodenum proximal to that boundary.
学校使用十二指肠空肠交界附近Treitz韧带的经典边界；其近端的食管、胃及十二指肠属于上消化道来源。

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:09.264
In that classic framework, distal bowel is grouped as lower. Contemporary resources often discuss small-bowel bleeding separately from colonic and rectal lower bleeding.
经典框架把远端肠道统称下消化道；当代资源常把小肠出血，与结肠直肠的下消化道出血分开。

00:01:09.264 --> 00:01:20.496
Know which framework the school question is using, but do not let the label overstate a field diagnosis. The receiving team benefits from the actual vomit and stool description.
应知道学校题目采用哪种框架，但不能让标签夸大现场诊断；接收团队更需要真实呕吐物及粪便描述。

00:01:20.496 --> 00:01:28.848
A boundary helps organize likely causes. It does not make the blood color a reliable map or determine how sick the person is.
边界帮助整理可能病因，却不会使血色变成可靠地图，也不能据此判断病情轻重。

00:01:28.848 --> 00:01:41.424
Hematemesis means vomiting blood. Fresh red material and coffee-ground material can both be important; coffee grounds reflect altered blood, often after contact with gastric contents.
Hematemesis指呕血。鲜红及咖啡渣样物都可能重要；咖啡渣反映血液被改变，常经历与胃内容物接触。

00:01:41.424 --> 00:01:52.608
Melena is black, tarry stool associated with digested blood. It commonly suggests an upper source, but does not prove one exact site or that bleeding has stopped.
Melena是与消化后的血相关的黑色柏油样便，常提示上消化道来源，却不证明某个确切部位，也不证明已止血。

00:01:52.608 --> 00:02:02.520
Hematochezia describes red or maroon rectal blood. Although often lower, a brisk upper bleed can move rapidly and appear this way.
Hematochezia描述鲜红或暗红直肠血，虽常来自下消化道，但大量快速上消化道出血也可如此。

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:14.520
Ask whether the finding was observed or reported, and note possible nonblood color changes from foods or medicines. Describe uncertainty rather than declaring every dark stool melena.
要分清亲见还是自述，并注意食物药物可能改变颜色；应说明不确定，不能把每次深色便都称柏油样黑便。

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:26.928
Peptic ulcers can erode a vessel, with risks including Helicobacter pylori and NSAID exposure. A prior pattern of meal-related pain is not required before a serious bleed.
消化性溃疡可侵蚀血管，相关风险包括幽门螺杆菌及NSAID暴露；严重出血前不一定已有典型进食相关痛。

00:02:26.928 --> 00:02:38.736
Portal hypertension can produce enlarged esophageal or gastric veins. Rupture can cause major hemorrhage, and impaired liver function can complicate coagulation and recovery.
门静脉高压可使食管或胃静脉扩张，破裂可能大出血；肝功能受损还可使凝血及恢复更复杂。

00:02:38.736 --> 00:02:52.200
A Mallory-Weiss mucosal tear can follow forceful retching. It is different from a full-thickness esophageal rupture, which may present with severe chest or upper-abdominal pain and systemic deterioration.
Mallory-Weiss黏膜撕裂可在剧烈干呕后发生，不同于食管全层破裂；后者可能剧烈胸上腹痛并全身恶化。

00:02:52.200 --> 00:03:04.272
These histories refine suspicion, but absence of liver disease, alcohol use or known ulcers does not clear the patient. Treat the current airway and perfusion consequences.
这些病史帮助细化怀疑，但无肝病、饮酒或已知溃疡不能放行；需处理当前气道及灌注后果。

00:03:04.272 --> 00:03:15.792
Diverticular bleeding can be painless yet large. Pain severity and blood-loss severity are separate questions, so do not use a comfortable abdomen as a stability test.
憩室出血可能无痛但量大。疼痛程度与失血程度是不同问题，不能用腹部不痛作为稳定测试。

00:03:15.792 --> 00:03:28.752
Vascular lesions can bleed intermittently; inflammatory, ischemic or infectious colitis and malignancy have different patterns and risks. The field may not distinguish them definitively.
血管病变可间歇出血；炎症、缺血、感染性结肠炎及恶性病的模式风险各异，现场未必能确定区分。

00:03:28.752 --> 00:03:40.440
Hemorrhoids and fissures can produce bright red blood. A history of either does not explain away new heavy bleeding, fainting, poor perfusion or a major change from baseline.
痔及肛裂可鲜红出血，但有此病史，不能消除新大量出血、晕厥、低灌注或明显偏离基线的担忧。

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:51.000
Use the history to identify possibilities and risk. Avoid reassuring the patient that it is only hemorrhoids without appropriate assessment and follow-up.
应从病史识别可能性及风险；未经适当评估和后续安排，不能安慰说“只是痔疮”。

00:03:51.000 --> 00:04:01.008
Overt bleeding is visible. Occult bleeding is not visible to the eye and is commonly detected during evaluation of anemia or a positive stool test.
显性出血可以看见；隐性出血肉眼看不到，常在贫血评估或粪便检测阳性时被发现。

00:04:01.008 --> 00:04:13.032
Slow chronic loss can lead to fatigue, pallor, breathlessness and reduced exercise tolerance. A change may seem gradual until another illness reduces the remaining reserve.
缓慢长期丢失可造成疲倦、苍白、气促及活动耐量下降；变化可能一直缓慢，直到另一急病消耗剩余储备。

00:04:13.032 --> 00:04:24.144
A major acute bleed can also be unrecognized because the blood has not yet been seen or reported. Do not confuse that situation with proof of a small chronic occult loss.
严重急性出血也可能因尚未看见或报告而未被识别；不能据此认定只是少量慢性隐血。

00:04:24.144 --> 00:04:36.240
Shock findings with a compatible story require action without waiting for stool testing or visible blood. A field fecal test is not a prerequisite for stabilization or conveyance.
相符病史加休克表现，要求行动，不必等粪便检测或可见血；现场隐血测试不是稳定处理和转运的前提。

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:47.592
Blood loss can reduce venous return, ventricular filling and stroke volume. Sympathetic compensation may preserve cuff pressure through heart-rate and vascular changes.
失血可减少静脉回流、心室充盈及搏出量；交感代偿可能通过心率和血管变化维持袖带压。

00:04:47.592 --> 00:05:00.936
Look at the whole pattern: pallor, skin temperature, pulse quality, dizziness, weakness, respiratory change and mentation. A normal pressure does not prove adequate organ perfusion.
要看苍白、皮温、脉质、头晕、无力、呼吸变化及精神的整体模式；正常血压不证明器官灌注足够。

00:05:00.936 --> 00:05:11.256
Medicines, age, autonomic disease and baseline physiology can modify the pulse response. Absence of tachycardia cannot rule out hemorrhage.
药物、年龄、自主神经疾病及基线生理，可改变脉搏反应；没有心动过速也不能排除失血。

00:05:11.256 --> 00:05:23.208
Do not force the patient to stand to demonstrate orthostatic change or assign an exact blood-loss percentage from one observation. Use a safe supported move and repeat meaningful measurements.
不能强迫站起来证明体位变化，也不能从一项观察估精确失血百分比；应安全有支撑搬动并重复有意义测量。

00:05:23.208 --> 00:05:33.648
Pulse oximetry estimates saturation of available hemoglobin. It does not measure how much hemoglobin is present or how much blood is reaching tissues.
脉搏血氧估计可用血红蛋白的饱和程度，不测血红蛋白总量，也不测多少血真正到达组织。

00:05:33.648 --> 00:05:45.480
A patient with anemia or low circulating volume may have a normal saturation and poor oxygen delivery. Interpret the number with perfusion, function and the bleeding story.
贫血或循环容量少者，可能血氧正常但氧输送差；应结合灌注、功能和出血史解释读数。

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:58.608
In acute blood loss, an early hemoglobin concentration may initially appear acceptable before redistribution and fluid effects evolve. A single result cannot cancel ongoing hemorrhage concern.
急性失血早期，在再分布及液体效应展开前，血红蛋白浓度可能看似尚可；单次结果不能消除持续失血担忧。

00:05:58.608 --> 00:06:10.872
Give oxygen when indicated through the actual pathway and support ventilation if inadequate. Oxygen and crystalloid do not restore lost red-cell carrying capacity or stop the source.
需依真实路径有指征给氧，通气不足则支持通气；氧及晶体液不能恢复丢失的红细胞携氧量，也不能止住来源。

00:06:10.872 --> 00:06:21.696
Ask when the change began, how often blood or dark material appeared and whether it continues. Separate a witnessed event from a patient or companion report.
应问何时变化、血或深色物出现几次，以及是否持续；分清亲见事件与患者同行者报告。

00:06:21.696 --> 00:06:33.456
Ask about fainting, exertional breathlessness, chest discomfort, weakness and new confusion. These can reveal consequences even when the visible amount seems small.
需问晕厥、活动气促、胸部不适、无力及新混乱，即使可见量似乎少，也可能揭示后果。

00:06:33.456 --> 00:06:45.000
Review prior ulcer or bleeding, liver disease, renal or cardiac illness and recent vomiting. Do not require a classic past history before taking a new bleed seriously.
需复核溃疡出血史、肝病、肾心疾病及近期呕吐；不能强求典型旧史，才认真对待新出血。

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:59.472
Identify anticoagulants, antiplatelets and NSAIDs with the last known dose. Do not independently reverse or permanently discontinue a prescription; provide accurate information for urgent clinical review.
应确认抗凝、抗血小板及NSAIDs，并记上次已知剂量；不能独立逆转或永久停处方，应为紧急临床复核提供准确信息。

00:06:59.472 --> 00:07:09.576
A sixty-four-year-old reports several black tarry stools and increasing weakness. The history includes apixaban and recent nonprescription ibuprofen.
一位64岁者自述数次黑色柏油样便，且越来越无力，药史有阿哌沙班及近期非处方布洛芬。

00:07:09.576 --> 00:07:20.184
The patient is pale, with pulse one hundred ten, breathing twenty-four, pressure one hundred sixteen over seventy-two and saturation ninety-eight on room air.
患者苍白，脉110、呼吸24、血压116/72，室内空气血氧98%。

00:07:20.184 --> 00:07:30.408
The patient feels faint when trying to move. The preserved pressure and saturation do not cancel concern about gastrointestinal bleeding and impaired delivery.
患者尝试移动时近晕厥，保住的血压及血氧，不能消除胃肠出血和输送受损的担忧。

00:07:30.408 --> 00:07:42.288
State the immediate priorities before naming the presumed source: supported safe positioning, primary assessment, serial perfusion checks, indicated care and timely conveyance.
推测来源前应先说即时重点：安全有支撑体位、初步评估、连续灌注核查、有指征照护及及时转运。

00:07:42.288 --> 00:07:53.784
Do not stand this patient to prove an orthostatic result. Explain the concern and plan a supported movement with the team, appropriate monitoring and airway equipment available.
不能让这位患者站起证明体位结果；应解释担忧，并与团队计划有支撑搬动，备适当监测及气道设备。

00:07:53.784 --> 00:08:05.520
Repeat airway, breathing and circulation assessment, with relevant glucose and abdominal examination. Track pulse quality, mental status and pressure with times.
需重复气道呼吸循环评估，加相关血糖及腹部检查，带时刻追踪脉质、精神和血压。

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:16.512
Obtain indicated access and provide permitted support with reassessment. Do not delay conveyance for a perfect venous setup or to finish an arbitrary fluid volume.
需取得有指征通路并提供获准支持、复评；不能为完美静脉设置或输完任意液量延误转运。

00:08:16.512 --> 00:08:29.424
Pre-alert the receiving team with suspected bleeding, anticoagulant and NSAID history, faintness and actual observations. Leave the exact source uncertain unless there is evidence to establish it.
应向接收团队预警疑出血、抗凝及NSAID史、近晕厥与真实观察；没有确定证据时保留确切来源的不确定。

00:08:29.424 --> 00:08:40.248
Prepare suction, an emesis receptacle, suitable PPE and the airway equipment you can use. Active blood or vomit can rapidly alter the initial assessment.
应准备吸引、呕吐接器、适当PPE及可用气道设备；活动血液或呕吐可迅速改变初步评估。

00:08:40.248 --> 00:08:51.480
Use a supported, tolerated position and enable drainage if vomiting, with injury needs respected. A mask must not prevent immediate access to clear the airway.
应使用有支撑、可耐受体位，呕吐时便于引流并兼顾伤情；面罩不能阻碍立即清理气道。

00:08:51.480 --> 00:09:02.376
Check depth and effort as well as saturation. If ventilation is inadequate, provide effective support and early advanced help rather than waiting for a low oxygen number.
除了血氧，还需查深度及呼吸功；通气不足时应有效支持并及早高级援助，不能等氧数值低。

00:09:02.376 --> 00:09:14.544
No airway device guarantees protection against aspiration. Reassess clearance and ventilation after any change, especially with declining responsiveness or continuing hematemesis.
任何气道器械都不保证防误吸；每次改变后都需复评清除及通气，尤其反应下降或持续呕血时。

00:09:14.544 --> 00:09:24.696
Explain the examination, obtain the appropriate consent and protect dignity. Expose only what is needed and use a position the patient can tolerate.
应解释检查、取得适当同意并保护尊严，只暴露所需部分，采用患者可耐受体位。

00:09:24.696 --> 00:09:36.912
Observe distention, scars, symmetry and how movement affects pain. Gentle assessment can identify tenderness or guarding without repeatedly reproducing severe pain.
观察膨胀、疤痕、对称及活动如何影响疼痛；轻柔评估可发现压痛或肌防御，不必反复诱发剧痛。

00:09:36.912 --> 00:09:50.592
The old deep five-to-ten-centimeter rebound instruction is not a routine field maneuver. Do not repeatedly press a suspected pulsatile mass or require a digital rectal examination to justify urgent care.
旧书深压五至十厘米再查反跳痛，不是常规现场动作；不能反复按疑搏动包块，也不需先做肛诊才有理由紧急照护。

00:09:50.592 --> 00:10:02.208
Bowel sounds may add information but cannot clear obstruction or ischemia. Document what was actually assessed and let current instability take priority over a lengthy examination.
肠鸣音可增加信息，但不能排除梗阻或缺血；应记录真实检查，并让当前不稳定优先于冗长检查。

00:10:02.208 --> 00:10:12.936
Use serial observations with the frequency required by the patient and local standards. A changing pattern is more useful than one comfortable number copied forward.
应按患者和当地标准所需频率连续观察；变化模式比反复抄写一次放心数值更有用。

00:10:12.936 --> 00:10:23.640
Link each observation to the time, position and intervention. If the patient becomes confused or breathing worsens, repeat the primary assessment immediately.
每次观察都需连到时刻、体位及干预；混乱或呼吸恶化时，应立即重复初步评估。

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:35.352
Blood mixed with water, food or stool is difficult to quantify. Describe what you saw and give an honest estimate or uncertainty rather than a precise invented volume.
血混水、食物或粪便时难以定量；应描述所见并诚实估计或说明不确定，不能编精确体积。

00:10:35.352 --> 00:10:45.096
A small visible amount does not measure all hidden or previous loss. Likewise, a red toilet is not proof of a particular number of liters.
少量可见血不能衡量全部隐匿或此前丢失；同样，便池变红也不能证明某个升数。

00:10:45.096 --> 00:10:55.272
GI hemorrhage cannot usually be controlled by external pressure. Arrange timely definitive evaluation while supporting the current circulation and breathing.
胃肠出血通常不能靠外压控制，应在支持当前循环和呼吸的同时安排及时确定评估。

00:10:55.272 --> 00:11:05.568
Use indicated vascular access and the actual local fluid plan, comparing mentation, pulses, pressure and respiratory function after each step.
应取得有指征通路并依真实当地液体计划，每一步后比较精神、脉搏、血压及呼吸功能。

00:11:05.568 --> 00:11:19.392
Crystalloid can support volume temporarily, but excess can dilute and worsen congestion. It does not replace red cells or close a bleeding vessel, so an empty bag is not the treatment endpoint.
晶体液可暂时支持容量，但过量可稀释并加重淤血；它不替代红细胞，也不关闭出血血管，因此袋空不是治疗终点。

00:11:19.392 --> 00:11:30.816
The hospital may need blood support, endoscopic treatment or another source-control process. Communicate risk early rather than allowing minor setup tasks to consume that time.
医院可能需要血液支持、内镜治疗或其他来源控制，应及早传风险，不能让次要设置消耗这些时间。

00:11:30.816 --> 00:11:43.344
Appropriate analgesia need not be withheld because it supposedly masks all abdominal disease. Symptom relief supports humane care while examination and reassessment continue.
不必因为所谓会掩盖全部腹病就拒绝适当镇痛；症状缓解支持人道照护，同时继续检查和复评。

00:11:43.344 --> 00:11:58.464
Choose only an authorized option suitable for this patient. Active bleeding, kidney disease, allergy, interactions, impaired breathing and pressure can all matter; hypotension is not the only possible contraindication.
只能选择获准且适合本人的方案；活动出血、肾病、过敏、相互作用、呼吸及血压都重要，低压并非唯一可能禁忌。

00:11:58.464 --> 00:12:09.264
Gross abdominal distention is a current nitrous-oxide contraindication. Do not use a familiar pain medicine automatically just because it worked on a previous patient.
明显腹胀是当前氧化亚氮禁忌，不能只因以前对别人有效，就自动给熟悉止痛药。

00:12:09.264 --> 00:12:21.864
Use the indicated antiemetic and reassess, but prepare for vomiting despite treatment. Improvement of pain or nausea does not prove the dangerous underlying problem has resolved.
需使用有指征止吐药并复评，但即使治疗仍要备呕吐；痛或恶心改善，不证明危险基础问题已解决。

00:12:21.864 --> 00:12:32.832
The currently checked BCEHS tranexamic-acid monograph explicitly lists nontraumatic gastrointestinal hemorrhage, such as a bleeding ulcer or varices, as a contraindication.
当前核对BCEHS氨甲环酸专论，明确把溃疡或静脉曲张等非创伤胃肠出血列为禁忌。

00:12:32.832 --> 00:12:42.384
Do not borrow the trauma or maternal indication merely because this patient is bleeding. Cause-specific eligibility remains necessary.
不能只因患者在出血，就借用创伤或母体适应证；仍需病因特定资格。

00:12:42.384 --> 00:12:56.352
The original HALT-IT trial did not demonstrate a reduction in bleeding death with its studied regimen and found more venous thromboembolic events. This supports avoiding a uniform all-bleeding treatment assumption.
HALT-IT原试验的研究方案未显示减少出血死亡，并发现更多静脉血栓栓塞事件，支持避免“所有出血都同治”的假设。

00:12:56.352 --> 00:13:06.384
Continue the indicated basic support, consultation and urgent conveyance plan. An old textbook statement about occasional use is not current permission.
应继续有指征基础支持、咨询及紧急转运计划；旧教材“有时使用”的句子，不是当前许可。

00:13:06.384 --> 00:13:16.512
A mechanical obstruction physically limits passage. Causes can be within the lumen, in the bowel wall or outside it, including adhesions from prior surgery.
机械梗阻是实际限制通行，可在腔内、肠壁或外部形成，例如以前手术后的粘连。

00:13:16.512 --> 00:13:25.200
A hernia can trap bowel, and a twisted segment or closed loop can threaten the blood supply as well as the passage of contents.
疝可能嵌住肠段，扭转或闭袢除了阻挡内容物，还可能威胁血供。

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:37.920
Fluid and gas collect upstream, increasing distention and vomiting risk. The location and completeness influence the pattern, but field symptoms cannot define the anatomy precisely.
液体及气体在上游积聚，增加膨胀及呕吐风险；部位和完整程度影响模式，但现场症状不能精确确定解剖。

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:46.584
Ask about prior surgery, hernia and previous obstruction. A patient without those histories can still have a serious obstruction.
需问手术、疝及梗阻史，但没有这些病史，仍可能发生严重梗阻。

00:13:46.584 --> 00:13:58.848
Functional ileus means impaired bowel propulsion without a single physical blockage. Surgery, systemic illness, medicines and electrolyte problems can contribute.
功能性肠麻痹指没有单个实际堵点却推进受损，可由手术、全身病、药物及电解质问题促成。

00:13:58.848 --> 00:14:11.736
Distention, discomfort, nausea, vomiting and reduced bowel output can resemble mechanical obstruction. Quiet bowel sounds do not establish which mechanism is present.
膨胀、不适、恶心、呕吐和肠输出减少可像机械梗阻；安静肠鸣音不能确定哪种机制。

00:14:11.736 --> 00:14:23.232
Both need evaluation in the right clinical context, with immediate support for airway, perfusion and other deterioration. Do not assume the functional label makes the patient safe.
两者都需结合背景评估，并即时支持气道、灌注及其他恶化；不能因为叫“功能性”就认为安全。

00:14:23.232 --> 00:14:33.192
The school small-versus-large pattern comparison is useful preparation. Keep it separate from claiming that examination alone has excluded a surgical cause.
学校小肠与大肠模式比较很有帮助，但不能据此声称仅靠检查就排除了外科病因。

00:14:33.192 --> 00:14:44.808
Small-bowel obstruction often relates to adhesions or hernia. Crampy pain reflects contractions against resistance, and vomiting may be an early prominent symptom.
小肠梗阻常与粘连或疝有关；绞痛反映肠道对阻力收缩，呕吐可能早期就很突出。

00:14:44.808 --> 00:14:56.088
The more proximal the obstruction, the less dramatic the abdominal distention may initially be. A flat-looking abdomen cannot exclude a dangerous upper small-bowel problem.
梗阻越靠近近端，最初腹胀可能越不明显；外观看似平坦，不能排除危险近端小肠问题。

00:14:56.088 --> 00:15:08.064
Losses through vomiting and sequestration can reduce effective volume. Ask about intake, emesis, urine and the time course rather than only counting visible episodes.
呕吐及液体滞留可减少有效容量，需问摄入、呕吐、尿量及病程，而不只数可见次数。

00:15:08.064 --> 00:15:19.056
A change from intermittent cramps to severe continuous pain is concerning, especially with tenderness or poor perfusion. It is not necessary to wait for feculent vomiting.
间歇绞痛转为严重持续痛很危险，尤其伴压痛或低灌注；无需等粪样呕吐才行动。

00:15:19.056 --> 00:15:30.432
Large-bowel obstruction can relate to a colorectal tumor, a volvulus or a stricture. There may be a gradual bowel-habit change, although some causes present suddenly.
大肠梗阻可能来自结直肠肿瘤、扭转或狭窄，可有渐进排便改变，但某些病因也会突然发生。

00:15:30.432 --> 00:15:40.464
Distention is often marked, with reduced stool or flatus. Vomiting may be less prominent early than in a proximal small-bowel obstruction.
腹胀常明显，伴排便或排气减少；与近端小肠梗阻相比，初期呕吐可能较不突出。

00:15:40.464 --> 00:15:52.224
These are tendencies, not a checklist that safely identifies the segment. Severe distention and deterioration can require urgent evaluation even with little vomiting.
这些只是倾向，不是可安全定位肠段的清单；即使呕吐少，明显腹胀及恶化也可能需紧急评估。

00:15:52.224 --> 00:16:03.072
Do not label large-bowel obstruction slow and therefore safe. Ischemia, perforation, aspiration and shock can occur in either broad category.
不能把大肠梗阻称为慢所以安全；两大类都可能缺血、穿孔、误吸及休克。

00:16:03.072 --> 00:16:15.480
Partial obstruction may permit some passage, and stool already beyond a new blockage can still be passed. A recent bowel movement or a small episode of diarrhea does not exclude obstruction.
部分梗阻可能允许一些内容物通过，而新堵点远端原有粪便也仍可排出；近期排便或少量腹泻不能排除梗阻。

00:16:15.480 --> 00:16:27.264
Similarly, hearing bowel sounds does not prove normal passage, while not hearing them briefly does not establish paralysis. The noisy environment further limits confidence.
同样，听到肠鸣不证明通行正常，短时没听到也不证明肠麻痹；嘈杂环境还会降低判断把握。

00:16:27.264 --> 00:16:37.584
Ask about the last normal stool and flatus, not only whether anything passed. Compare that with distention, pain, vomiting, surgery and the clinical trend.
应问上次正常排便和排气，而不只是有没有排过，并与膨胀、痛、呕吐、手术及临床趋势比较。

00:16:37.584 --> 00:16:47.064
Do not delay necessary transport for prolonged auscultation or assume symptom improvement after an antiemetic has removed a mechanical problem.
不能为长时间听诊延误必要转运，也不能认为止吐后症状改善就移除了机械问题。

00:16:47.064 --> 00:16:57.552
The gut normally handles large amounts of fluid through secretion and absorption. Obstruction changes movement and absorption, with fluid accumulating upstream.
肠道平常通过分泌和吸收处理大量液体；梗阻改变移动及吸收，使液体在上游积聚。

00:16:57.552 --> 00:17:08.520
Fluid can become sequestered in the lumen and edematous bowel wall. The school calls this third spacing: fluid is unavailable to maintain effective circulation.
液体可滞留肠腔及水肿肠壁；学校称为第三间隙，意思是这些液体不能用于维持有效循环。

00:17:08.520 --> 00:17:18.552
Vomiting adds external water and electrolyte loss. A distended abdomen therefore does not prove the person has sufficient circulating volume.
呕吐还增加外部水及电解质丢失，因此腹部膨大不能证明循环容量足够。

00:17:18.552 --> 00:17:31.368
Assess perfusion and breathing, and provide only the indicated response-directed support. The diagram explains risk; it does not prescribe one fluid dose for every distended patient.
需评灌注呼吸，仅给予有指征、依反应支持。图示解释风险，并不为所有腹胀者规定同一补液量。

00:17:31.368 --> 00:17:41.568
Increasing pressure or a trapped loop can impede venous drainage. Swelling can further impair perfusion, and arterial supply may become inadequate.
压力增高或肠袢受困，可阻碍静脉引流；水肿又可进一步损灌注，并使动脉供血不足。

00:17:41.568 --> 00:17:53.400
This can produce ischemia and eventually tissue necrosis. A strangulated hernia or closed-loop process may threaten blood flow before the typical full symptom pattern appears.
这可能造成缺血，最终组织坏死。绞窄疝或闭袢可能在典型全套症状出现前就威胁血流。

00:17:53.400 --> 00:18:07.776
Concerning change includes severe continuous pain, tenderness, guarding, worsening perfusion or altered function. Normal temperature and a soft abdomen do not guarantee that ischemia is absent.
危险变化包括严重持续痛、压痛、防御、灌注恶化或功能变化；正常温度及柔软腹部不能保证没有缺血。

00:18:07.776 --> 00:18:19.320
The field task is urgent recognition and escalation, not proving every surgical mechanism. Do not force a painful hernia back or wait for a dramatic late abdomen.
现场任务是紧急识别及升级，不是证明每种外科机制；不能强推疼痛疝回去，也不能等晚期戏剧性腹征。

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:32.256
A compromised bowel wall can perforate, allowing irritating contents and bacteria into the peritoneal cavity. Peritonitis is inflammation of that lining and can have several causes.
肠壁受损可穿孔，使刺激性内容物及细菌进入腹膜腔。腹膜炎指该衬层炎症，可能有多种原因。

00:18:32.256 --> 00:18:42.960
Pain may become persistent and worsen with movement, with tenderness or guarding. Do not deliberately reproduce repeated rebound pain to prove the emergency.
疼痛可转持续并随活动加重，伴压痛或防御；不能反复刻意诱发反跳痛来证明急症。

00:18:42.960 --> 00:18:55.512
Inflammation, leakage, infection and poor circulation can overlap. A patient may be deteriorating before fever, rigid abdomen or critical hypotension becomes obvious.
炎症、漏出、感染和低循环可重叠；发热、板状腹或危急低压明显前，患者可能已在恶化。

00:18:55.512 --> 00:19:07.320
Request appropriate help, prepare airway and perfusion support and notify the receiving team early. Absence of one classic sign should not postpone definitive assessment.
应取得适当帮助，备气道灌注支持并及早通知接收团队；缺一个典型征象，不能推迟确定评估。

00:19:07.320 --> 00:19:17.472
Establish the pain onset and whether cramps have changed to persistent severe pain. Ask how vomiting, distention and output evolved together.
应建立痛起始、绞痛是否转持续剧痛，并问呕吐、膨胀及输出如何共同变化。

00:19:17.472 --> 00:19:29.424
Ask about the last normal stool and flatus, the character of vomit, intake and urine. Avoid treating one bowel movement or one normal temperature as reassurance.
需问上次正常排便排气、呕吐物特征、摄入及尿量；不能用一次排便或一次正常体温就放心。

00:19:29.424 --> 00:19:42.456
Ask about surgery, hernia, cancer, ostomy and prior episodes, with the actual baseline. The patient may know their anatomy and device plan better than a generic label describes.
需问手术、疝、癌、造口及既往发作，并了解真实基线；患者对本人解剖及器械计划的了解，可能比通用标签更准确。

00:19:42.456 --> 00:19:54.840
Review illness and medication changes, especially agents that affect motility or fluid balance. Use this information to refine the problem, not to declare its cause from a single clue.
应复核疾病药物变化，尤其影响肠动力或液体平衡者；这些用于细化问题，不能靠单一线索确定病因。

00:19:54.840 --> 00:20:05.208
A fifty-three-year-old with prior abdominal surgery has crampy pain, repeated vomiting and increasing distention. There was a small loose stool eight hours ago.
一位53岁腹部手术史患者，绞痛、反复呕吐并越来越胀，八小时前排过少量稀便。

00:20:05.208 --> 00:20:15.672
Now flatus and urine are reduced. Pulse is one hundred twelve, pressure one hundred eight over sixty-eight and temperature thirty-seven point one.
现在排气及尿量减少，脉112、血压108/68、体温37.1℃。

00:20:15.672 --> 00:20:26.160
The small stool does not exclude partial or newly developing obstruction. The loss history and reduced urine raise concern about effective volume and renal perfusion.
少量便不能排除部分或新发展梗阻，丢失史及尿少增加对有效容量和肾灌注的担忧。

00:20:26.160 --> 00:20:40.008
Assess current ABCs, perfusion, pain and relevant glucose/rhythm, support safely and arrange timely evaluation. Do not give a laxative or a trial meal to test the diagnosis.
需查当前ABC、灌注、痛及相关血糖节律，安全支持并及时评估；不能用泻药或试吃一餐来测试诊断。

00:20:40.008 --> 00:20:53.592
During preparation, pain becomes severe and constant, tenderness increases and the patient looks paler. Pulse rises to one hundred twenty-four and pressure falls to ninety-six over sixty.
准备期间疼痛转严重持续，压痛增加且更苍白；脉升124、血压降96/60。

00:20:53.592 --> 00:21:05.760
This worsening trend matters more than the earlier normal temperature or small stool. Possible ischemia, perforation, volume loss and another cause must remain open.
该恶化趋势比先前正常温度或少量便重要；需保留可能缺血、穿孔、容量丢失及其他病因。

00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:17.496
Repeat the primary assessment, provide indicated support and seek advanced resources without delaying urgent conveyance. Update the receiving team with the change and concern.
应重复初步评估、有指征支持并取得高级资源，不能延误紧急转运；需把变化及担忧更新给接收团队。

00:21:17.496 --> 00:21:28.608
A field label cannot establish whether surgery is needed. The safe decision is urgent definitive assessment, with actual treatment and response documented en route.
现场标签不能确定是否需要手术；安全决定是紧急确定评估，并在途中记录真实处理及反应。

00:21:28.608 --> 00:21:40.848
Prepare for further vomiting with suction and safe positioning. Assess airway protection and effective ventilation repeatedly, especially if the patient becomes fatigued or confused.
需用吸引及安全体位备再次呕吐，反复评气道保护和有效通气，尤其出现疲劳或混乱时。

00:21:40.848 --> 00:21:52.752
Use indicated access and fluid support according to the current local plan. Reassess perfusion and breathing because congestion risk or another diagnosis may alter the response.
应依现行当地计划取得有指征通路及液体支持；需复评灌注呼吸，因为淤血风险或另一诊断可能改变反应。

00:21:52.752 --> 00:22:04.584
Provide authorized, appropriate symptom relief rather than withholding all medication out of fear of masking. Improvement of nausea does not remove the need for evaluation.
应给予获准、合适症状缓解，而不是怕掩盖就停全部药；恶心改善并不取消进一步评估需要。

00:22:04.584 --> 00:22:18.792
Red flags such as persistent severe pain, peritoneal concern, shock or altered function require early escalation and notification. Definitive decompression or surgery belongs to the appropriate clinical setting.
持续剧痛、腹膜担忧、休克或功能改变等红旗，需及早升级及通知；确定减压或手术属于适当临床环境。

00:22:18.792 --> 00:22:28.968
Withhold routine food and drink in suspected obstruction or active vomiting while arranging clinical evaluation. Do not try to flush the blockage with water.
疑梗阻或活动呕吐时，安排临床评估期间需暂停常规进食饮水；不能试图用水冲开堵塞。

00:22:28.968 --> 00:22:40.128
Do not improvise laxatives, enemas or forceful reduction of a painful hernia. A suspected blockage needs proper evaluation, not a trial to provoke output.
不能自创泻药、灌肠或强行推回疼痛疝；疑堵塞需要正确评估，不是试着刺激排出。

00:22:40.128 --> 00:22:51.264
Gross distention excludes nitrous oxide in current local guidance. Hospital NG decompression is not a blanket independent PCP insertion instruction.
当前当地指导对明显膨胀排除氧化亚氮；医院鼻胃管减压并非普遍PCP独立置管指令。

00:22:51.264 --> 00:23:03.648
Nothing-by-mouth precautions do not mean ignoring a separate time-critical threat. Use the appropriate safe route and clinical advice for essential indicated treatment, including a glucose emergency.
禁食预防并不代表忽视另一个时间敏感威胁；对必要有指征治疗，包括血糖急症，应使用适当安全途径及临床建议。

00:23:03.648 --> 00:23:15.216
Ask about the actual device, purpose and normal output. An ileostomy, colostomy, urinary diversion, catheter or feeding tube does not tell you the whole anatomy from its name.
需问真实器械、用途及正常输出；回肠造口、结肠造口、尿路改道、导尿管或喂养管的名称，都不能说明全部解剖。

00:23:15.216 --> 00:23:25.176
Trace visible tubing and check for traction, a kink or a collection problem within your competence. Reassess the patient even if one external problem is found.
应在能力内沿可见管线查看牵拉、扭折或收集问题；即使发现一个外部问题，仍需复评患者。

00:23:25.176 --> 00:23:36.768
Do not break a closed system, feed through an unverified tube or remove a drain simply to simplify transport. Secure and support the actual system according to its plan.
不能为了方便转运而破封闭系统、经未核位置管喂入，或移除引流；需依实际计划固定支撑系统。

00:23:36.768 --> 00:23:50.136
A new cessation of output with pain, distention, bleeding or deterioration needs urgent review. The paired CPSC guide connects these observations with safe transfer and device boundaries.
新停止输出并伴痛、胀、出血或恶化，需要紧急复核；配套CPSC导引把这些观察与安全转移和器械边界连接。

00:23:50.136 --> 00:24:02.376
Abdominal symptoms can arise from aortic disease, impaired bowel blood flow or another vascular emergency. A pulsatile mass or unequal arm pressures are not mandatory findings.
腹部症状可来自主动脉病、肠血流受损或其他血管急症；搏动包块或双臂压差不是必须发现。

00:24:02.376 --> 00:24:17.280
ACS can present with epigastric discomfort, nausea or weakness. Obtain indicated ECG and cardiac assessment without assuming every abdominal patient should automatically receive aspirin or nitrate.
ACS可表现为上腹不适、恶心或无力；应有指征查心电及心脏，但不能每位腹痛者自动给阿司匹林或硝酸酯。

00:24:17.280 --> 00:24:29.136
Consider pregnancy-related bleeding, pelvic disease, urinary retention and renal illness when relevant. Ask respectfully about the actual anatomy, dates and symptoms.
相关时需考虑妊娠出血、盆腔病、尿潴留及肾病，并尊重地问真实解剖、日期和症状。

00:24:29.136 --> 00:24:41.712
Check glucose when indicated and keep infection and other metabolic causes open. A GI symptom label cannot explain away new focal neurology or impaired consciousness.
有指征时需查血糖，并保留感染及其他代谢病因；胃肠标签不能消除新局灶神经征或意识受损的担忧。

00:24:41.712 --> 00:24:54.000
Older, immunosuppressed or neuropathic patients may have less obvious pain, fever or abdominal signs. A subtle examination can coexist with serious disease.
较年长、免疫抑制或神经病变患者，痛、发热或腹征可能不明显；检查轻微也可能伴严重病。

00:24:54.000 --> 00:25:03.696
Cardiac, kidney and liver disease can reduce reserve and complicate fluids or medicines. Ask what has changed from the individual baseline.
心、肾及肝病可降低储备，并使补液或用药复杂；应问相对本人基线改变了什么。

00:25:03.696 --> 00:25:15.792
Use accessible communication and appropriate interpretation, with a chosen support person when agreed. Do not equate difficulty giving a history with incapacity or dismiss the report.
需采用可及沟通及适当口译，经同意可加入选定支持人员；不能把采史困难等同无决定能力，或因此轻视报告。

00:25:15.792 --> 00:25:27.864
Support dignity during soiling or vomiting and document factual findings. Treatment urgency should reflect clinical need rather than age stereotypes or embarrassment about symptoms.
污染或呕吐时应保护尊严并客观记录；紧迫性应来自临床需要，而非年龄刻板印象或症状带来的羞耻。

00:25:27.864 --> 00:25:39.984
A bleed can reduce effective volume and renal perfusion. Obstruction can add vomiting and sequestration, producing a similar urine-history clue through a different initial mechanism.
出血可减少有效容量和肾灌注；梗阻可增加呕吐和滞留，通过不同起始机制产生类似尿史线索。

00:25:39.984 --> 00:25:49.752
If ischemia or perforation develops, inflammation and infection can add. Do not assume that one shock label contains the entire explanation.
若出现缺血或穿孔，又可能增加炎症及感染；不能认为单一休克标签就是完整解释。

00:25:49.752 --> 00:26:02.040
The priorities remain current airway, ventilation and perfusion, with cause-sensitive permitted care and prompt definitive evaluation. Response must be measured, not promised.
重点仍是当前气道、通气、灌注，结合病因敏感的获准照护及及时确定评估；反应需要测量，不能承诺。

00:26:02.040 --> 00:26:14.280
Ask What Else when findings or response do not fit. Examples include aortic disease, cardiac ischemia, ectopic bleeding, glucose disturbance or a toxic exposure.
发现或反应不符时应问What Else，例如主动脉病、心肌缺血、异位妊娠出血、血糖异常或毒性暴露。

00:26:14.280 --> 00:26:23.568
Lead with the current concern, such as suspected GI hemorrhage with near-syncope or possible obstruction with worsening constant pain and perfusion.
先说当前担忧，例如疑胃肠出血伴近晕厥，或疑梗阻伴持续痛及灌注恶化。

00:26:23.568 --> 00:26:33.456
Include the symptom timeline, medicines, comorbidities and actual loss description. Make clear which findings were observed and which were reported.
应包括症状时间线、药物、共病及真实丢失描述，并明确亲见与自述。

00:26:33.456 --> 00:26:46.224
State serial values and function, the interventions with times and the actual response. A pressure trend and change in mentation can be more useful than an invented source certainty.
要说连续数值、功能、处理时刻及真实反应；血压趋势和精神变化，比自创来源确定性更有用。

00:26:46.224 --> 00:26:57.168
Give the arrival estimate and requested preparation, with remaining uncertainty. Update the alert if bleeding, breathing or perfusion changes during conveyance.
需给预计到达及所需准备，并说明剩余不确定；途中出血、呼吸或灌注改变时，要更新预警。

00:26:57.168 --> 00:27:07.800
For the bleeding case, explain why melena supports concern but does not prove a source, and why normal pressure and saturation do not establish adequate delivery.
对出血病例，应解释柏油样便为何支持担忧却不能证明来源，以及正常血压和血氧为何不证明输送足够。

00:27:07.800 --> 00:27:17.832
For the obstruction case, explain why a recent small stool does not clear it, and how a larger bowel can be accompanied by reduced effective circulating volume.
对梗阻病例，应解释近期少量便为何不能排除，以及更大的肠管为何可能伴更少有效循环容量。

00:27:17.832 --> 00:27:28.152
State the safe examination, immediate support, medication checks and transport priority. Include an action you will avoid and the specific reason.
应说安全检查、即时支持、药物核查和转运重点，并加一个应避免的行动及具体原因。

00:27:28.152 --> 00:27:40.224
Then explain how worsening constant pain, altered function, new airway difficulty or a poor response changes urgency. Use the paired reading to repair any missing mechanism.
再解释持续痛恶化、功能变、新气道困难或反应差如何改变紧迫性，利用配套阅读补漏掉的机制。

00:27:40.224 --> 00:28:28.440
Correct the source drop-factor unit: tubing calibration is drops per milliliter, not drops per minute. For gravity, drops/minute equals milliliters/hour times drops/milliliter divided by sixty. Original calculation: an authorized 87 mL/hour through a verified 15 drops/mL set gives 21.75, approximately 22 drops/minute using the trained rounding method. Count over a full minute and verify the patient and delivered volume. A pump uses mL/hour; do not enter 22 as its rate or infer the set calibration from its appearance. An arithmetic answer does not establish that fluid is indicated.
应纠正来源滴系数单位：输液器标定为每毫升多少滴，而不是每分钟多少滴。重力滴速为每小时毫升数乘每毫升滴数，再除60。原创计算：获准速度87mL/小时，确认输液器为15滴/mL，得到21.75，按受训取整方法约22滴/分钟。应计满一分钟，并核对患者及实际输入量。泵使用mL/小时，不能把22填成泵速度，也不能凭外观猜滴系数。算术正确不证明患者有补液指征。

00:28:28.440 --> 00:29:10.608
Gravity flow changes with bag height, patient position, bends, lumen diameter, viscosity, clamp movement and infiltration. Reassess after the arm or stretcher moves; an initially correct clamp setting is not a guarantee. The dated source TKVO20-50 mL/hour, fixed cannula-change intervals and 24-hour bag statements are source/agency examples, not one universal field rate or a proof of sterility until a deadline. Distinguish product expiry, time since access and contamination. Clinical condition, actual device instructions and the prescribed plan determine action.
重力流速会受液袋高度、患者体位、弯折、管腔直径、黏度、夹具移动及浸润影响。手臂或担架移动后应复评，最初夹具调对不保证之后仍准确。旧来源TKVO每小时20至50mL、固定换留置针时段及液袋24小时描述，都是来源或机构例子，不是统一院前速度，也不保证截止时刻前必然无菌。应区分产品有效期、接入后时间及污染；行动由临床情况、真实器械说明和处方计划决定。

00:29:10.608 --> 00:30:00.456
If a transfusion reaction is suspected, stop the suspected transfusion and obtain the immediate clinical/transfusion-service response while supporting ABCs. Preserve necessary vascular access using the authorized compatible plan; do not flush the remaining suspect blood into the patient. Recheck identity, document product/times/symptoms/response and preserve the bag/set for the investigation process. The source mild-fever continuation note is not permission to continue or restart without assessment and an explicit treating-team plan. Its IV-epinephrine equipment sentence is not an ordinary PCP IV epinephrine order; use the actual local pathway for a recognized anaphylactic threat.
疑似输血反应时，应停止可疑输注，立即取得临床及输血服务响应，同时支持ABC。按获准相容方案维持必要血管通路，不能把剩余可疑血液冲入患者。复核身份，记录产品、时间、症状及反应，并依调查流程保留液袋和管路。来源轻度发热可继续的注释，不允许未经评估和明确治疗团队计划就继续或重启；其准备静脉肾上腺素一句，也不是普通PCP静脉给药医嘱，已识别的过敏性威胁应依真实本地路径处理。

00:30:00.456 --> 00:30:43.056
Original integration: a patient with abdominal illness, a central line and a nutrition infusion develops a new fever and reduced responsiveness during transfer. Do not assume the line alone proves bloodstream infection or that stopping every infusion is harmless. Support immediate physiology, check glucose, compare actual baseline and inspect the visible system. Obtain a trained plan for any suspected source or critical-infusion interruption and arrange urgent evaluation. Handover includes every route/product/rate, last known normal function, new findings, actions, response and remaining uncertainty.
原创整合：腹部疾病患者带中央管及营养输注，转运时出现新发热和反应下降。有中央管不证明一定血流感染，停掉所有输注也不一定无害。应支持即时生理、查血糖、比较真实基线并检查可见系统。对可疑感染源或关键输注中断，应取得受训计划并安排紧急评估。交接包括每条途径的产品速度、最后正常功能、新发现、已做行动、反应及未决不确定性。

00:30:43.056 --> 00:30:53.304
You should now describe the school upper/lower bleeding framework, major causes, overt and occult loss and important exceptions to color-based assumptions.
现在应能描述学校上下消化道框架、主要原因、显隐性丢失，以及便色推断的重要例外。

00:30:53.304 --> 00:31:05.544
You should compare small and large bowel patterns, explain third spacing and recognize possible ischemia, perforation and systemic deterioration without demanding every classic sign.
应能比较小大肠模式、解释第三间隙，并在不强求全部典型征象时识别可能缺血、穿孔及全身恶化。

00:31:05.544 --> 00:31:16.872
Your care plan should protect airway and perfusion, relieve symptoms safely, avoid unnecessary provocation and use the actual local drug and procedure boundaries.
照护计划应保护气道灌注、安全缓解症状、避免不必要诱发，并使用真实当地药物操作边界。

00:31:16.872 --> 00:31:28.992
Finish with an accurate changing-patient handover and the bilingual reading, then move to the school endocrine and integrated medical requirements. Practical competence still needs supervised performance.
最后完成准确动态交接及中英阅读，再进入学校内分泌和综合医学要求；实际操作能力仍需督导表现。
